<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Paladin Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic for Phase 4. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, reputation rewards, and the new 10 &amp; 25-man Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot-gear">Protection Paladin Tank Best in Slot Gear, Gems, and Enchants - Pre-Raid Phase 4</h2>Frankly the primary thing you're strongly advised to do is to maintain crit immunity through -5.6% crit suppression, this is obtained through either 540 defense skill, or a combination of resilience and defense. Mostly everything else is just window dressing, though even crit immunity is optional on entry-level raid encounters, so in reality just try to get as close to this value as possible while also maximizing your health pool for 10-man normal raid encounters.<br/>
<br/>The new dungeon difficulty Titan Rune Gamma is implemented in phase 4, it will be accessible through the Random Dungeon Finder and the unique currency is <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2711/defilers-scourgestone">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defiler's Scourgestone</span></span></a>, obtained at the rate of one per dungeon boss. <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=2711/defilers-scourgestone">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defiler's Scourgestone</span></span></a> can be used to purchase a 25-man normal <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>, 25-man hardmode <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> as well as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49908/primordial-saronite">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_felflamebreath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordial Saronite</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a>. Gamma dungeons will also award <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47241/emblem-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></a> giving you full access to the 245 item level tier 9 and a huge array of very servicable gear from previous content phases. Alongside the more grindy aspects of gearing up, you will also be awarded with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a> through daily and weekly activities that are used to purchase tier 10 and 264 item level gear.<br/>
<br/>When you hit 80 and is just starting out, gearing can be a daunting task for anyone, but especially tanks. We have a higher degree of responsibility put on us to not only have the correct gear, but also a good idea of what we're doing and it is expected of us to a certain degree to be capable of soft leading or outright guiding groups through dungeons. If this character is your first and only level 80 that you have, we suggest that you continue questing in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=210/icecrown">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=67/the-storm-peaks">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Storm Peaks</span></a> as quests here will award you <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40752/emblem-of-heroism">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_proclaimchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Heroism</span></a>, gold, and reputation. None of these things will compete with endgame or even dungeon loot, though gearing is like climbing a ladder and you will have to start somewhere. Keep an eye out for the tournament dailies, these can also be done for some surefire upgrades above questing gear.<br/>
<br/>While the amount of tokens required to farm all of these items is daunting, we want to stress that it is by no means necessary to have this full set before engaging with larger group size content like raids, this is simply an illustrative article meant to showcase what you can build without raiding. Likewise tanking gear can be very flexible once you understand that matching the basic criteria of being uncrittable and having a respectable health pool means you can mix and match a lot of equipment, the items here are configured as a set and does not rule out other items that are potentially strong sidegrades or even in a vacuum upgrades on a slot per slot basis.<br/>
<br/>
